                        "question": "Can I cook acidic foods in my Smithey?",
                        "answer": "<p>Yes! You can absolutely cook acidic foods in your Smithey. Dishes made with ingredients like tomatoes, lemons, or vinegar may strip or discolor the seasoning, especially on a newer skillet before the seasoning has fully matured. This is completely normal and nothing to worry about—you can simply re-season your Smithey and keep cooking. As your seasoning continues to develop, acidic foods will have less of an effect on the cooking surface.</p>",
